==English==

===Etymology===
{{named-after|en|Gerard Kuiper|wplink=Gerard Kuiper}}, who theorized about the belt's existence.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkaɪpəɹ/|nocount=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[Kuiper belt]] [[object]]}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} A type of [[trans-Neptunian object]] (TNO) (a certain type of [[minor planet]]) that has an orbit in the Kuiper belt (between 30-50 AU) with [[inclination|inclinations]] consistent with the [[ecliptic]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|KBO}}
* {{l|en|kuiperoid}}

